raphsOfPathwidthLe_le_flipWeighted\",\n\"\"\" + ''.join(f'    \"{n}\",\\n' for n in new_names) + \")\"),\n])\n\n# E. paper\nedit('paper1/latex/sec9e_appendix_random.tex', [\n(\"Lean~\\\\leanref{theoremCl}, the independence step on paper), and its constant\",\n \"Lean~\\\\leanref{theoremCl}, the independence step by a product over disjoint\\nblocks of pairs, in Lean~\\\\leanref{theoremClproduct}), and its constant\"),\n(\"\"\"theorem with its inner probability as a finite weighted count; of the\nclosed-pair count, the union bound and the characterisation of a closed pair\nare in Lean and the independence step is on paper; the constants\"\"\",\n\"\"\"theorem with its inner probability as a finite weighted count; the\nclosed-pair count is a Lean theorem in both its pair-summed and its\nsize-summed form, with the independence step a product over disjoint blocks\nof pairs; the constants\"\"\"),\n])\nedit('paper1/latex/sec9a_appendix_lean.tex', [\n(\"\"\"the evaluation of each term as $(1-p)^{|A||R|}\\\\bigl((1-(1-p)^{|A|})(1-(1-p)^{|R|})\\\\bigr)^{|S|}$ is on paper} \\\\leannames{weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_closedPairs} \\\\\\\\\"\"\",\n\"\"\"each term evaluated in the next row} \\\\leannames{weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_closedPairs} \\\\\\\\\n\\\\leanentry{theoremClproduct}{The closed-pair count, the independence step: the $p$-weight of the subsets of a set of pairs that satisfy one predicate on each of pairwise disjoint blocks is the product of the per-block weights (the pairs in no block are free), so the $G(n,p)$ probability that $(A,R)$ is closed is exactly $(1-p)^{|A||R|}\\\\bigl((1-(1-p)^{|A|})(1-(1-p)^{|R|})\\\\bigr)^{|S|}$ (one block of the forbidden $A$--$R$ pairs, two star blocks per $v\\\\in S$); hence $\\\\Pr[\\\\pw\\\\le k]\\\\le\\\\sum_{a\\\\ge t,\\\\,r'\\\\ge r}\\\\binom na\\\\binom{n-a}{r'}(1-p)^{ar'}\\\\bigl((1-(1-p)^{a})(1-(1-p)^{r'})\\\\bigr)^{n-a-r'}$, the expected number of closed pairs of at least the forced sizes} \\\\leanname