"+## 13. Reserve: Theorem Cl's independence step, and Theorem Cl in full, in Lean (item 13, 2026-11-01)","+","+**Question.** Of the gaps items 01–12 left (§0.9), which one closes in a","+session, and does it close? The item named three kinds of candidate: a","+killed item's cheapest surviving variant, a Lean statement left as a named","+`Prop`, the planted measurement at one larger `n`.","+","+**Why this one.** The near-threshold constants at finer `c` were already","+done by item 09's (d) branch (§9.6, eleven `c` from 2.0 to 4.0). The","+cover-model partition sum for `E_bip` needs the component law of a random","+intersection graph, which no held paper gives (§7.4, (H_C)), so it would be","+a measurement with no theorem at its end. The planted measurement at","+`n = 48–64` addresses the two unreconciled instruments (§0.9 item 3) but","+costs 2–5 core-hours of Harper plus an enumeration whose tail cost is","+unbounded (item 04 censored 7 instances at `n ≤ 32`), and at best narrows a","+disagreement between two statistics measured at different `k`. No statement","+was left as a named `Prop` (§10.7), but §10.3 named the product-over-blocks","+lemma as \"the only thing between Theorem Cl and Lean\", §0.9 listed it first,","+and iterations 10 and 12 both pointed the reserve at it. It is deterministic,","+needs no compute, is checked by the gate, and changes a sentence in the","+paper from \"on paper\" to \"in Lean\". That is the item.","+","+### 13.1 What is proved","+","+All in `lean/MOSPFormalization/SeparatorMoment.lean`, sections","+`ProductOverBlocks` and `ClosedProduct`; 22 new `theorem` declarations and 4","+definitions (the file: 100 theorems, 25 definitions, 1,683 lines); no","+`sorry`, no `axiom`; every new theorem on `propext`, `Classical.choice`,","+`Quot.sound` only (`paper1/axiom_check.lean`, eleven new lines; `make -C","+paper1/latex axioms`: 307 theorems checked, 0 failures).","+","+* **The split lemma** (`sum_subsetWeight_split`). For disjoint finsets `B`,","+  `T'` of any type and predicates `P`, `Q`,","+","+      Σ_{F ⊆ B ∪ T', P(F ∩ B) ∧ Q(F ∩ T')} p^|F| (1 − p)^{|B ∪ T'| − |F|}","+        = (Σ_{F ⊆ B, P F} p^|F| (1 − p)^{|B| − |F|}) · (Σ_{F ⊆ T', Q F} p^|F| (1 − p)^{|T'| − |F|}),","+","+  by the bijection `F ↦ (F ∩ B, F ∩ T')` with inverse `(F₁, F₂) ↦ F₁ ∪ F₂`","+  (`sum_nbij'`), the weight splitting as `subsetWeight_union`.","+* **The product over blocks** (`sum_subsetWeight_blocks`). For a finset `s`","+  of block indices, blocks `B i ⊆ T` pairwise disjoint on `s`, and predicates","+  `P i`,","+","+      Σ_{F ⊆ T, ∀ i ∈ s, P i (F ∩ B i)} p^|F| (1 − p)^{|T| − |F|}","+        = Π_{i ∈ s} Σ_{F ⊆ B i, P i F} p^|F| (1 − p)^{|B i| − |F|},","+","+  by induction on `s`: the split lemma peels one block off (`T = B i ∪ (T ∖ B i)`),","+  and the remaining blocks lie inside `T ∖ B i`; the base case is the","+  binomial identity `Σ_{F ⊆ T} p^|F| (1 − p)^{|T| − |F|} = 1`","+  (`sum_subsetWeight_powerset`). The free pairs are what this base case","+  absorbs: no `piFinset` bijection and no `prod_univ_sum`, which §10.3 had","+  priced at a session.","+* **The block weights** (`sum_subsetWeight_eq_empty`,","+  `sum_subsetWeight_nonempty`): \"no pair chosen\" weighs `(1 − p)^|B|`, \"some","+  pair chosen\" weighs `1 − (1 − p)^|B|`.","+* **The closed pair as an edge-set predicate**. `starPairs A v` is the set of","+  pairs `s(a, v)`, `a ∈ A` (`card_starPairs`: `|A|` of them;","+  `starPairs_subset_top` for `v ∉ A`); `ClosedEdgeSet A R F` is \"`F` meets no","+  forbidden `A`–`R` pair, and for every `v ∉ A ∪ R` meets `starPairs A v` and","+  `starPairs R v`\"; `isClosedPair_iff_closedEdgeSet`: a pair is closed iff","+  its sides are disjoint and the edge set is a closed edge set (through","+  `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both` of item 10, `isEmptyPair_iff_inter_forbidden`","+  and `exists_adj_iff_inter_starPairs_nonempty`);","+  `image_edges_closedPairGraphs`: `edges` maps the graphs in which `(A, R)` is","+  closed onto the closed edge sets. The disjointness of the blocks is three","+  small `Sym2.eq_iff` case splits (`disjoint_starPairs_forbidden`,","+  `disjoint_starPairs_starPairs`, `disjoint_starPairs_of_ne`).","+* **The independence step** (`sum_gnpWeight_closedPairGraphs`). For disjoint","+  `A`, `R` and `S = V ∖ (A ∪ R)`,","+","+      Σ_{G : (A, R) closed in G} gnpWeight p G","+        = (1 − p)^{|A||R|} · ((1 − (1 − p)^|A|)(1 − (1 − p)^|R|))^{|S|},","+","+  exactly, for every real `p`: the forbidden pairs are one block with the","+  predicate \"empty\", and each `v ∈ S` contributes the block","+  `starPairs A v ∪ starPairs R v` with the predicate \"meets both stars\",","+  whose weight is the split lemma again (`sum_subsetWeight_starBlock`); the","+  pairs inside `A`, inside `R` and inside `S` are the free ones.","+* **Theorem Cl, pair-summed** (`weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_closedPairCount`):","+  for `0 ≤ p ≤ 1`, `k < n`,","+","+      Σ_{pw G ≤ k} gnpWeight p G ≤ Σ_{(A, R) ∈ closedIndices t r} (1 − p)^{|A||R|} ((1 − (1 − p)^|A|)(1 − (1 − p)^|R|))^{|V ∖ (A ∪ R)|},","+","+  the union bound of item 10 with every term evaluated.","+* **Theorem Cl, size-summed** (`weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_closedPairFormula`):","+  the same with the right-hand side regrouped over the size pairs `(a, r')`,","+  `t ≤ a`, `r ≤ r'`, `a, r' ≤ n`:","+","+      Σ_{(a, r')} C(n, a) · C(n − a, r') · (1 − p)^{a r'} ((1 − (1 − p)^a)(1 − (1 − p)^{r'}))^{n − a − r'},","+","+  by `closedIndices_eq_biUnion` (the closed indices are the disjoint union","+  of the exact-size index sets `pairIndices a r'`) and `sum_closedIndices_eq`","+  (each fibre has `C(n, a) C(n − a, r')` elements, `card_pairIndices` of item","+  10). The binomial product is `n!/(a! r'! s!)`, `s = n − a − r'`, the","+  multinomial §8.1 writes; terms with `a + r' > n` are zero through","+  `C(n − a, r') = 0`. This is §8.1's Theorem Cl verbatim, up to that spelling","+  of the multinomial.","+","+### 13.2 Checked before it was stated","+","+`reports/scratch/separator_moment/13_reserve/check.py` (`check.log`, 6 s):","+in exact rationals at `p = 1/2` and `1/3`, (1) the per-pair identity on","+**every disjoint ordered pair of every labelled graph on `n = 1–5`** (363","+pairs, up to 1,024 graphs each) and 80 random pairs at `n = 6` (32,768","+graphs each); (2) the split lemma and the blocks lemma on 300 random","+instances each (random finsets of size `≤ 7–8`, random blocks, predicates","+given as random subsets of the powerset — not monotone, not symmetric). **Zero","+violations.** Theorem Cl's size-summed formula was already equal to the","+enumerated `E[X₃]` on every labelled graph at `n ≤ 7` (item 08, §8.3). The","+test `test_closed_pair_probability_is_the_product_over_blocks` keeps the","+per-pair identity at `n ≤ 4` in full and 40 pairs at `n = 5`, and the","+size-summed sum against `closed_count_exact`;","+`test_item13_names_are_audited_and_declared` pins the eleven names to","+`learning.sandwich.SEPARATOR_PROVED`, the Lean file and the axiom audit.","+","+### 13.3 What it cost, and what the record had estimated","+","+§10.3 priced the lemma at \"a session on its own\" and sketched it through","+`Finset.prod_univ_sum` and a bijection `𝒫(T) ≅ piFinset (𝒫 ∘ B) × 𝒫(T ∖ ⋃ B)`.","+The proof here is the induction above; the first build had nine errors (two","+renamed Mathlib lemmas, `eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem` and `notMem_empty`;","+`Disjoint.inter_eq` is not the Finset lemma, `disjoint_iff_inter_eq_empty`","+is; an unneeded `and_assoc`; a lemma stated with one hypothesis too many;","+and a decidability-instance mismatch — `Fintype.decidableForallFintype`","+against `decidableDforallFinset` — when `filter_congr` meets a bounded `∀`","+over a finset of a `Fintype`, settled by `ext` and `mem_filter`), the second","+two, the third none; the size-summed form built first time. About twelve","+minutes of Lean after the check; the file builds in 1.5 s. Compute: none.","+The paper: `sec9e_appendix_random.tex` now says the independence step is in","+Lean (two sentences), `sec9a_appendix_lean.tex` has a row A.69","+(`theoremClproduct`) with the five headline names; `make -C paper1/latex","+check`: no undefined references, 74 pages; `check_axioms`: 198 names cited,","+0 without an axiom line, 307 theorems, 0 failures. §0.2, §0.7, §0.9, §10.3","+and the `CLAUDE.md` paragraph of §12 are patched with a pointer here;","+§8.4 and §10.1 are kept as their items wrote them.","+","+### 13.4 Regenerate, size range, kill verdict, what this does not claim","+","+* **Regenerate.** `cd lean && lake build`;","+  `python3 reports/scratch/separator_moment/13_reserve/check.py`;","+  `python3 -m pytest tests/test_separator_moment.py -k \"closed_pair_probability or item13 or proved_names\"`;","+  `make -C paper1/latex && make -C paper1/latex check && make -C paper1/latex axioms`;","+  `python -m learning.sandwich --stage separator --out /tmp/sandwich.md`","+  (the `--out` keeps `reports/sandwich_tables.md` as the full run wrote it).","+  Logs: `reports/scratch/separator_moment/13_reserve/` (`check.log`,","+  `lake_build.log`, `axiom_check.log`, `gate.log`).","+* **Size range.** The theorems hold for every finite `V`, every `k < n`, and","+  every real `p` for the identity, `0 ≤ p ≤ 1` for the inequalities (Lean,","+  no size). The checks: `n ≤ 6`.","+* **Kill verdict: none** (the item had none; the deliverable is a proof). The","+  check that precedes the statement found nothing, as §8.3 had.","+* **Does not claim.** Anything about `β_closed`: it is still the root of a","+  closed-form exponent computed numerically (§6.1 (b)), and the passage from","+  the finite formula to the exponent (Stirling, the supremum at the corner)","+  is on paper. Theorem Cl-cover and Lemma J (inclusion–exclusion over pattern","+  sets), Lemmas P, G, F and Corollary S′ (components as finsets), and the","+  evaluation of the flip-weighted count stay on paper, with their obstacles","+  as §10.3 names them. The two unreconciled instruments of §0.9 item 3 are","+  untouched. Nothing re-solved; `solutions/` untouched; no compute."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/separator_moment.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014rpe9WiqfPXRRsLqKANj28","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
